# mikehoffmann.co — Entrepreneurship Collective
#
# Signups need the ActiveCampaign block below. Until it is set, the form
# returns a visible "not connected yet" error instead of a success screen it
# cannot honour. Set these in the Vercel project's Environment Variables, not
# in a committed file.

# ── ActiveCampaign (the newsletter platform) ───────────────────────────────
# API_URL and API_KEY are both on Settings → Developer in ActiveCampaign.
# The URL is the account's own host, with no trailing slash and no /api/3.
# ACTIVECAMPAIGN_API_URL=https://youraccount.api-us1.com
# ACTIVECAMPAIGN_API_KEY=
# LIST_ID is the numeric id of the Entrepreneurship Collective list — it is
# the `listid` query parameter when you open that list in the AC dashboard.
# ACTIVECAMPAIGN_LIST_ID=

# Optional. Stamps which block on the page sent the signup (hero or closing)
# onto an AC custom field, so you can see which CTA converts. The value is the
# numeric field id from Settings → Fields. Skipped when unset.
# ACTIVECAMPAIGN_SOURCE_FIELD_ID=

# Optional. Applies a tag to every signup from this site. Numeric tag id.
# ACTIVECAMPAIGN_TAG_ID=

# ── Escape hatch: anything else, via webhook (Zapier / Make / n8n) ─────────
# Only used when the ActiveCampaign variables above are absent. Receives
# { email, source, publication, submitted_at } as JSON.
# SUBSCRIBE_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Canonical origin. Only needed before the custom domain is attached — once
# mikehoffmann.co is on the project, Vercel supplies it automatically.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://mikehoffmann.co
